# This is a byte-exact reconstruction project. Git must not rewrite anything.
#
# The sources are 1990s DOS files staged into a DOSBox build, and the release
# in DEMOVT15/ is someone else's shipped archive. In both cases the bytes on disk
# ARE the artefact, so line-ending and encoding conversion is disabled outright
# rather than negotiated. `-text` means: never convert on checkin or checkout.

# --- everything, by default: leave the bytes alone ------------------------
* -text

# --- DOCUMENTS ARE LF -----------------------------------------------------
# Markdown is not read by any DOS tool, so it has no reason to carry CRLF.
# `text eol=lf` normalises it on the way in and checks it out LF everywhere,
# which is the one place in this repo where letting git convert is correct.
*.md    text eol=lf

# --- but let git diff the DOS files, without ever converting them ---------
# `diff` without `text` gives readable diffs while still never touching EOLs.
*.py    -text diff
*.PAS   -text diff
*.ASM   -text diff
*.INC   -text diff
*.pas   -text diff
*.asm   -text diff
*.inc   -text diff
*.TXT   -text diff
*.CFG   -text diff
*.BAT   -text diff
*.conf  -text diff

# --- genuinely binary: never try -----------------------------------------
*.EXE   binary
*.TPU   binary
*.OBJ   binary
*.TP    binary
*.VTO   binary
*.bin   binary
